  "question": {
    "text": "A cavity of radius <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></math> is made inside a solid sphere. The volume charge density of the remaining sphere is <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">ρ</mi></math>. An electron (charge <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">e</mi></math>, mass <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mi></math>) is released from rest inside the cavity from point <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">P</mi></math> as shown in the figure. The centre of the sphere and centre of the cavity are separated by a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>. The time after which the electron again touches the sphere is<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image36-1ff5e67b-a143-4a57-8569-ffbf3d162a27.jpg\" style=\"height: 151px; width: 150px;\" />",
