  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />acceleration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mi>e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/435212.png\" style=\"width: 140px; height: 140px;\" />&nbsp; &amp;&nbsp;<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-07-11_at_4.49.17_PM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 171px;\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mi>e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>r</mi></math></p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><p>The electron will move opposite to electronic field with constant acceleration along shown horizontal line of length <math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo><msqrt> <mn>2</m